hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27591","Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sasah, from Yaqub ibn Abi Yaqub, from Umm al-Mundhir bint Qays al-Ansariyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me, with him Ali, and Ali was convalescing from illness, and we had hanging clusters of dates. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood eating from them, and Ali stood eating from them. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept saying to Ali: Stop, you are convalescing, until he refrained. She said: I made barley and chard and brought it. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Ali: Take from this, for it is more beneficial for you."
"27592","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Yaqub ibn Abi Yaqub, from Umm al-Mundhir al-Adawiyyah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me, with him Ali, and Ali was convalescing, and he mentioned the hadith, except he said: Then I made for them chard and barley. My father said: And likewise Fazarah ibn Amr said: chard."
"27593","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sasah al-Ansari, from Yaqub ibn Abi Yaqub, from Umm al-Mundhir bint Qays, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me, with him Ali ibn Abi Talib, and Ali was convalescing from illness. She said: We had hanging clusters, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Ali stood eating from them. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept saying: Slowly, for you are convalescing, until Ali refrained. She said: I had made barley and chard, and when we brought it, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Ali: Take from this, for it is more suitable for you. They ate that."
